{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776709224,"nonce":"k4w+qBC/sprNFsZxmtAUiiJuOc8=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABACr9jA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/61","origin":"github"},"title":"Show RTK fix type in GPS annunciator instead of satellite count","message":"The GPS annunciator entry currently shows satellite count (e.g., \"34.0\"), which is somewhat useful. However, for operations the RTK fix type (none / float / fixed) is much more valuable — it tells the operator whether they have centimeter-level positioning.\n\nThe fix type is available from mavros GPS topics. The annunciator config or a diagnostic node should surface this.\n\nDiscovered during 2026-04-20 deployment session.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null}]}